<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Inaba Province</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Inaba Province was an old province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-japan">Sea of Japan</a> coast, corresponding to the eastern part of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tottori-prefecture">Tottori Prefecture</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edo-period">Edo period</a> it formed, with neighbouring Hōki, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tottori">Tottori</a> Domain of the Ikeda family. Under the Meiji reforms it became part of Tottori Prefecture in 1871.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/inaba-province.jpg" alt="Inaba Province" width="320" height="335" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ash_Crow · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Provinces_of_Japan-Inaba.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
